# Global Engineering & Product Rules (Goethe A2 Reading Simulator)

1. Scope & Constraints
   - The application **MUST run 100 % offline** once installed (PWA-ready, no external APIs).
   - All data (user creds, progress, tasks) lives in `localStorage` or IndexedDB. No backend.
   - Provide one demo credential pair: **admin / admin**.
   - Exam tasks are generated client-side from embedded JSON/YAML fixtures; keep them A2-level.
   - Mock API layer (`~/composables/api.ts`) to simulate REST; integrate latency simulation.
   - Use latest **Nuxt 3 (stable)** with TypeScript.
   - State management: **Pinia** (idempotent, persisted).
   - Styling: Tailwind CSS + Nuxt UI for polished, accessible design.
   - Total points system follows PRD (20 pts).

2. File-Size & Maintainability
   - Any **code file > 500 LOC MUST be split**.
   - Prefer functional decomposition over monoliths.
   - Keep rule files themselves ≤ 200 lines.

3. Documentation & Comments
   - **Always** comment non-trivial code using JSDoc-3.
   - Focus on **why/how**, not obvious **what**.
   - Do **NOT** delete useful legacy comments.

4. Quality Gates
   - ESLint + Prettier enforced in CI (airbnb-vue base).
   - Vitest unit tests cover critical logic (≥ 80 % lines).

5. Investigation Discipline
   - Thoroughly inspect every request: search, grep, docs (Context7) **before coding**.
   - Keep `README_PRD.txt` in sync: tick completed features. 
   - PRD is the single source of truth. Update it after every major milestone.

6. Performance & PWA
   - Register Service Worker via Nuxt PWA module (offline caching).
   - Code-split by route & component; lazy-import heavy assets.
   - Images compressed & optimized through `nuxt/image`.

7. Security
   - Store hashed demo password (bcrypt) even offline.
   - XSS protection via auto-escaping (Vue) & sanitising dynamic HTML.
   - Use CSP meta tags.

8. Accessibility (A11y)
   - WCAG 2.1 AA minimum.
   - Keyboard navigation for all interactive elements.
   - ARIA roles & focus management after route changes.

9. Versioning & Dependencies
   - Lock Node LTS (≥ 18) & exact package versions in `package.json`.
   - Use `pnpm` for deterministic installs (workspace).
